WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A colour analogue photograph, 10.2 x 15.2 cm, horizontal format, depicts her smiling.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.925
I’m not sure who captured her, but I still own the point-and-shoot Charman AW-750 camera, a ’90s relic I keep as memorabilia.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:19.315
Her lips, slightly tinted blue, hint at where my anemia came from, and so do the two sweaters she’s wearing, despite what appears to be late spring; everyone else in the photo is wearing summer clothes.

00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:25.960
This is the only known photograph of her outside the apartment, before the police began knocking on doors and escorting people to the border.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:31.255
In all other photographs, taken later, she is sitting on her couch, either staring at the camera or chasing me.

00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:38.800
I am usually out of frame or blurred, unaware that, in the register of the nation-state, our roles have been swapped. Only, she is not blurred; she is invisible.
